{"2305.15171":{"abstract":"Novel view synthesis via Neural Radiance Fields (NeRFs) or 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) typically necessitates dense observations with hundreds of input images to circumvent artifacts. We introduce Deceptive-NeRF/3DGS to enhance sparse-view reconstruction with only a limited set of input images, by leveraging a diffusion model pre-trained from multiview datasets. Different from using diffusion priors to regularize representation optimization, our method directly uses diffusion-generated images to train NeRF/3DGS as if they were real input views. Specifically, we propose a deceptive diffusion model turning noisy images rendered from few-view reconstructions into high-quality photorealistic pseudo-observations. To resolve consistency among pseudo-observations and real input views, we develop an uncertainty measure to guide the diffusion model's generation. Our system progressively incorporates diffusion-generated pseudo-observations into the training image sets, ultimately densifying the sparse input observations by 5 to 10 times. Extensive experiments across diverse and challenging datasets validate that our approach outperforms existing state-of-the-art methods and is capable of synthesizing novel views with super-resolution in the few-view setting.","arxiv_doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2305.15171","arxiv_id":"2305.15171","authors":["Xinhang Liu","Jiaben Chen","Shiu-hong Kao","Yu-Wing Tai","Chi-Keung Tang"],"categories":["Generative Priors & 3D Reconstruction"],"citation_count":45,"citation_fetched_at":"2026-11-11T04:46:40.793522+00:00","citation_status":"ok","code_url":null,"comment":"Paper accepted to ECCV 2024. Project page: https://xinhangliu.com/deceptive-nerf-3dgs","date_placement":"observed","db_citation_count":13,"db_citations":["2402.10259","2404.15891","2407.17418","2409.14316","2411.10947","2503.01774","2504.19261","2507.15690","2508.14717","2509.19073","2605.14135","cvf:Bao_Free360_Layered_Gaussian_Splatting_for_Unbounded_360-Degree_View_Synthesis_from_CVPR_2025_paper","cvf:Li_EVPGS_Enhanced_View_Prior_Guidance_for_Splatting-based_Extrapolated_View_Synthesis_CVPR_2025_paper"],"db_references":["2103.13415","2201.05989","paper:2023-49bc7a3f60","paper:2023-70a2202d04","paper:2024-be14b98be1"],"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-72640-8_19","first_author":"Liu et al.","huggingface":{"fetched_at":null,"last_attempt_at":"2026-11-12T19:03:05.123471+00:00","linked_spaces":null,"linked_spaces_complete":null,"linked_spaces_total":null,"project_page_evidence":null,"provider_ai_summary":null,"provider_summary":null,"repository_evidence":null,"source_url":"https://huggingface.co/papers/2305.15171","stars":null,"status":"not_found","submitted_on_daily_at":null,"upvotes":null},"id":"2305.15171","influential_citation_count":0,"metadata_evidence":{"published_date":[{"observed_at":null,"reviewed_at":null,"reviewed_by":null,"source":"arxiv","source_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15171v4","value":"2023-05-24"}],"venue":[{"observed_at":null,"reviewed_at":null,"reviewed_by":null,"source":"author_comment","source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15171","value":"ECCV 2024"}]},"month":5,"openalex_id":"https://openalex.org/W4403842239","paper_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.15171","pdf_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.15171.pdf","primary_arxiv_category":"cs.CV","primary_category":"Generative Priors & 3D Reconstruction","project_url":null,"publication_date":null,"publication_date_precision":"unknown","publication_year":null,"published_date":"2023-05-24","published_date_precision":"day","referenced_works":["https://openalex.org/W174941419","https://openalex.org/W2133665775","https://openalex.org/W2594519801","https://openalex.org/W2962785568","https://openalex.org/W2964288609","https://openalex.org/W3097660860","https://openalex.org/W3109476562","https://openalex.org/W3109585842","https://openalex.org/W3114462840","https://openalex.org/W3136327392","https://openalex.org/W3136656704","https://openalex.org/W3139743318","https://openalex.org/W3153167526","https://openalex.org/W3158035011","https://openalex.org/W3163847416","https://openalex.org/W3176368002","https://openalex.org/W3196466825","https://openalex.org/W3203312108","https://openalex.org/W3203583526","https://openalex.org/W3204859697","https://openalex.org/W3214712237","https://openalex.org/W3215589927","https://openalex.org/W3215769467","https://openalex.org/W3216476011","https://openalex.org/W3217184254","https://openalex.org/W4221151978","https://openalex.org/W4225672218","https://openalex.org/W4286759403","https://openalex.org/W4289785095","https://openalex.org/W4310895557","https://openalex.org/W4312234520","https://openalex.org/W4312325284","https://openalex.org/W4312926154","https://openalex.org/W4312933868","https://openalex.org/W4312969460","https://openalex.org/W4312971576","https://openalex.org/W4312986363","https://openalex.org/W4313154783","https://openalex.org/W4313196659","https://openalex.org/W4321471917","https://openalex.org/W4367692212","https://openalex.org/W4378450585","https://openalex.org/W4380486915","https://openalex.org/W4383108793","https://openalex.org/W4385318467","https://openalex.org/W4386065515","https://openalex.org/W4386065790","https://openalex.org/W4386065887","https://openalex.org/W4386065960","https://openalex.org/W4386066233","https://openalex.org/W4386066359","https://openalex.org/W4386071682","https://openalex.org/W4386075614","https://openalex.org/W4386075787","https://openalex.org/W4386075846","https://openalex.org/W4386075859","https://openalex.org/W4386076018","https://openalex.org/W4386076286","https://openalex.org/W4386076472","https://openalex.org/W4386080645","https://openalex.org/W4390872170","https://openalex.org/W4390872696","https://openalex.org/W4390873054","https://openalex.org/W4390873331","https://openalex.org/W4390873915","https://openalex.org/W4390874571","https://openalex.org/W4390889720","https://openalex.org/W4402667896","https://openalex.org/W4402727310","https://openalex.org/W4402774473","https://openalex.org/W4413116041","https://openalex.org/W569478347","https://openalex.org/W6600002382"],"reviewed_benchmark_cells":[],"source":"arxiv","tags":["Diffusion","Sparse-View","Foundations"],"title":"Deceptive-NeRF/3DGS: Diffusion-Generated Pseudo-Observations for High-Quality Sparse-View Reconstruction","tldr":"Introduces Deceptive-NeRF/3DGS to enhance sparse-view reconstruction with only a limited set of input images, by leveraging a diffusion model pre-trained from multiview datasets.","updated_date":"2024-07-15","venue":"ECCV 2024","year":2023},"2305.20082":{"abstract":"We introduce Control4D, an innovative framework for editing dynamic 4D portraits using text instructions. Our method addresses the prevalent challenges in 4D editing, notably the inefficiencies of existing 4D representations and the inconsistent editing effect caused by diffusion-based editors. We first propose GaussianPlanes, a novel 4D representation that makes Gaussian Splatting more structured by applying plane-based decomposition in 3D space and time. This enhances both efficiency and robustness in 4D editing. Furthermore, we propose to leverage a 4D generator to learn a more continuous generation space from inconsistent edited images produced by the diffusion-based editor, which effectively improves the consistency and quality of 4D editing. Comprehensive evaluation demonstrates the superiority of Control4D, including significantly reduced training time, high-quality rendering, and spatial-temporal consistency in 4D portrait editing. The link to our project website is https://control4darxiv.github.io.","arxiv_doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2305.20082","arxiv_id":"2305.20082","authors":["Ruizhi Shao","Jingxiang Sun","Cheng Peng","Zerong Zheng","Boyao Zhou","Hongwen Zhang","Yebin Liu"],"categories":["Generative Priors & 3D Reconstruction","Dynamic & 4DGS"],"citation_count":65,"citation_fetched_at":"2026-11-11T04:46:40.793522+00:00","citation_status":"ok","code_url":null,"comment":"The link to our project website is https://control4darxiv.github.io","date_placement":"observed","db_citation_count":20,"db_citations":["2311.14521","2312.00112","2312.02134","2312.04558","2402.07181","2404.04687","2405.03417","2406.09395","2407.17418","2410.05259","2410.07160","2412.01792","2501.07104","2501.09978","2501.12369","2510.01991","2510.19255","2511.20354","2601.01847","paper:2026-b6530448cc"],"db_references":["2308.09713","2309.16653","2310.08528","2311.12775","2311.16473","2312.02155","paper:2023-49bc7a3f60","paper:2023-70a2202d04"],"doi":"10.1109/cvpr52733.2024.00436","first_author":"Shao et al.","huggingface":{"fetched_at":"2026-11-12T19:03:05.123471+00:00","last_attempt_at":"2026-11-12T19:03:05.123471+00:00","linked_spaces":[],"linked_spaces_complete":true,"linked_spaces_total":0,"project_page_evidence":null,"provider_ai_summary":{"provider":"huggingface","source_url":"https://huggingface.co/papers/2305.20082","text":"Control4D uses a 2D diffusion-based editor within a 4D GAN framework to achieve high-fidelity and temporally consistent 4D portrait editing."},"provider_summary":{"provider":"huggingface","source_url":"https://huggingface.co/papers/2305.20082","text":"Recent years have witnessed considerable achievements in editing images with\ntext instructions. When applying these editors to dynamic scene editing, the\nnew-style scene tends to be temporally inconsistent due to the frame-by-frame\nnature of these 2D editors. To tackle this issue, we propose Control4D, a novel\napproach for high-fidelity and temporally consistent 4D portrait editing.\nControl4D is built upon an efficient 4D representation with a 2D\ndiffusion-based editor. Instead of using direct supervisions from the editor,\nour method learns a 4D GAN from it and avoids the inconsistent supervision\nsignals. Specifically, we employ a discriminator to learn the generation\ndistribution based on the edited images and then update the generator with the\ndiscrimination signals. For more stable training, multi-level information is\nextracted from the edited images and used to facilitate the learning of the\ngenerator. Experimental results show that Control4D surpasses previous\napproaches and achieves more photo-realistic and consistent 4D editing\nperformances. The link to our project website is\nhttps://control4darxiv.github.io."},"repository_evidence":null,"source_url":"https://huggingface.co/papers/2305.20082","stars":null,"status":"ok","submitted_on_daily_at":"2023-06-01T00:00:00.000Z","upvotes":2},"id":"2305.20082","influential_citation_count":0,"metadata_evidence":{"published_date":[{"observed_at":null,"reviewed_at":null,"reviewed_by":null,"source":"arxiv","source_url":"http://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20082v2","value":"2023-05-31"}]},"month":5,"openalex_id":"https://openalex.org/W4402733573","paper_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20082","pdf_url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2305.20082.pdf","primary_arxiv_category":"cs.CV","primary_category":"Generative Priors & 3D Reconstruction","project_url":"https://control4darxiv.github.io","publication_date":null,"publication_date_precision":"unknown","publication_year":null,"published_date":"2023-05-31","published_date_precision":"day","referenced_works":["https://openalex.org/W2129069237","https://openalex.org/W2546066744","https://openalex.org/W2612445135","https://openalex.org/W2739748921","https://openalex.org/W2889582485","https://openalex.org/W2933283236","https://openalex.org/W2963981733","https://openalex.org/W2995007867","https://openalex.org/W3008721991","https://openalex.org/W3036167779","https://openalex.org/W3096831136","https://openalex.org/W3109476562","https://openalex.org/W3114462840","https://openalex.org/W3135367836","https://openalex.org/W3161291858","https://openalex.org/W3162926177","https://openalex.org/W3163847416","https://openalex.org/W3173522942","https://openalex.org/W3174025609","https://openalex.org/W3176327543","https://openalex.org/W3177150392","https://openalex.org/W3184952021",